enting a specific objective or inquiry within the research.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'TRC 2 - financial corpus': {'type': ['DATASET'], 'description': ['A financial corpus used for pre-training the AWD-LSTM language model in ULMFit.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'label imbalance': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A challenge in the Financial PhraseBank dataset where the neutral sentiment class dominates, potentially impacting classification performance.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'Short Sentence Classification': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The task of classifying short sentences, which is a key focus of the performance comparison between FinBERT and other transfer learning methods.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'Accuracy': {'type': ['generic', 'generic', 'generic', 'generic'], 'description': ['A metric used to evaluate the performance of the models.', 'A metric used to evaluate the performance of the models.', 'The performance metric used to evaluate the sentiment analysis models, specifically mentioned as 0.96 for Vanilla BERT on a subset of the Financial Phrasebank dataset.', "A performance metric used to evaluate the model's performance, specifically in the context of sentiment analysis."], 'source_chunk_index': [8, 9, 10, 10]}, 'F1-score': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A metric used to evaluate the performance of the models.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'LPS': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A model used for comparison in the Financial PhraseBank dataset classification task.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'HSC': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A model used for comparison in the Financial PhraseBank dataset classification task.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'FinSSLX': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A model used for comparison in the Financial PhraseBank dataset classification task.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Dropout Probability': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The probability (p = 0.1) used for dropout regularization in the BERT implementation, which helps prevent overfitting.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Warm-up Proportion': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The proportion (0.2) of training steps used for the warm-up phase in the BERT implementation, which helps stabilize training.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Maximum Sequence Length': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The maximum length (64 tokens) of the input sequences used in the BERT implementation, which determines the context window for the model.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Learning Rate': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The learning rate (2e-05) used for training the BERT model, which controls the step size during optimization.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Mini-batch Size': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The mini-batch size (64) used during training, which determines the number of samples processed in each iteration.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Training Dataset Size': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['The size of the labeled training datasets used to measure the performance of the models.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'FinBERT - task': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['FinBERT further pre-trained on the classification training set.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'FinBERT - domain': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['FinBERT further pre-trained on a financial domain corpus (TRC 2 - financial).'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'Vanilla BERT': {'type': ['method', 'method'], 'description': ['BERT model without further pre-training.', 'A standard implementation of the BERT model, used as a baseline for comparison.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9, 10]}, 'Financial NLP': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The specific domain of NLP that FinBERT is designed for.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'Transformer Encoder Layers': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The architectural component within BERT, with 12 layers in the implemented model.'], 'source_chunk_index': [10]}, 'No adjustment (NA)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A setting used in the study to measure the performance of techniques against catastrophic forgetting, representing no specific adjustments to the model.'], 'source_chunk_index': [10]}, 'Slanted triangular learning rate and gradual unfreezing (STL+GU)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A combination of techniques used to optimize FinBERT, including slanted triangular learning rates and gradual unfreezing.'], 'source_chunk_index': [10]}, 'Named Entity Recognition': {'type': ['TASK', 'task'], 'description': ['A natural language processing task that FinBERT could be extended to.', 'A natural language processing task focused on identifying and classifying named entities (e.g., people, organizations, locations) within text.'], 'source_chunk_index': [11, 11]}, 'Reuters TRC-2 corpus': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A dataset shared by NIST, used in the study.'], 'source_chunk_index': [11]}, 'Sentiment Analysis': {'description': ["The process of computationally identifying and categorizing opinions expressed in a piece of text, especially to determine a writer's attitude with respect to a particular topic or document.", 'The primary task that FinBERT is designed to perform, specifically analyzing the sentiment expressed in financial texts.', 'The primary task of the study, which involves determining the sentiment (positive, negative, or neutral) expressed in financial text, specifically focusing on the sentiment of a sentence from a financial news article towards the financial actor depicted in the sentence.', 'The process of determining the emotional tone or attitude expressed within a text, particularly in the context of financial news.', 'The core NLP task that FinBERT is designed to perform on financial text.', 'The process of determining the emotional tone or attitude expressed within a text, a key application for FinBERT in the financial domain.'], 'type': ['task', 'TASK'], 'source_ch